{"id": "EUVD-2026-103540", "enisaUuid": "79a7f7b3-ef1b-3d06-8a06-d5941d6cb171", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Restrict CO-RE poisoning to relocatable instructions\n\nCO-RE relocation records can name any instruction offset. When a\nrelocation cannot be resolved, bpf_core_patch_insn() currently poisons its\ntarget before checking whether that instruction is a valid relocation\ntarget. Malformed metadata can therefore replace jumps, calls, exits,\nregister-source arithmetic, or non-immediate loads instead of failing at\nthe relocation step.\n\nHandle poisoning only after the instruction has passed the same class and\noperand-form checks used for a resolved relocation. Route invalid forms\nthrough the existing diagnostic and return a hard error. Keep poisoning\nsupported instructions, including both halves of a plain ldimm64, so an\nunresolved relocation in dead code remains valid.\n\nExtend bpf_core_poison_insn() to poison both halves of ldimm64, and return\nits status directly from each validated instruction case. This avoids\nrouting the success path through a common label and leaves the helper free\nto report errors.\n\nThe shared relocation code applies this restriction to both libbpf and\nin-kernel CO-RE.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:19:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:22:54", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a8c47e62d9aea2d47a09e06c1682c59c21b92449", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d3219c229d16900cef936adad28633c98946e432", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a0b79cdfcf34b53c85bac2d3cf022fc1342eeca0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f2a24101e89dd0804e717da7c1bd6af513698aa2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2d7d04357c41aa49a5ac658fcc207439f2ad6456", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8e4cbcca1e0a2fc5e6c8edb68e0cf5f2587f9319", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/394ae398337c5f87e567f6cd63b937fc2b2f6ddc"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7qcx-cmxq-wh7w", "CVE-2026-98626"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "135d2c0b-7ccc-3bfb-93d7-fa820d04fc7f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d7a252708dbc950ca2064310217e8b9f85846e2f <d3219c229d16900cef936adad28633c98946e432"}, {"id": "174df982-fa7c-38bc-b47b-4e6c5688bfb0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "18a56005-5e57-390d-9456-63ac7083b369", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.6"}, {"id": "266e34c8-ca63-379e-893e-a4351b5d581f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2a32798d-9883-33aa-8c1e-023a3b3f5816", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d7a252708dbc950ca2064310217e8b9f85846e2f <394ae398337c5f87e567f6cd63b937fc2b2f6ddc"}, {"id": "384aa683-ca9a-322b-b842-eea38c4e6089", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "3f0a6c88-1ed5-3e96-a309-70d68fa8abc0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5785a20c-23b0-3f4c-b32d-71e052ac2189", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "830f430e-b80b-383c-866a-b4f86b5499f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d7a252708dbc950ca2064310217e8b9f85846e2f <8e4cbcca1e0a2fc5e6c8edb68e0cf5f2587f9319"}, {"id": "90d76210-f27e-34c9-952e-58d7adc443b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d7a252708dbc950ca2064310217e8b9f85846e2f <2d7d04357c41aa49a5ac658fcc207439f2ad6456"}, {"id": "95a19a53-dca3-3b3d-847b-318b86a522ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d7a252708dbc950ca2064310217e8b9f85846e2f <a0b79cdfcf34b53c85bac2d3cf022fc1342eeca0"}, {"id": "bebb5504-efc7-3108-b980-41ba32281981", "pro